\cf0 This means the WT and B4 counts are 
\f0\b not the same kind of measurement
\f2\b0 . The WT call set is "everything that differs from the reference genome"; the B4 call set is "what is private to B4 after subtracting its matched WT parent". Because the B4 clone is 
\f7\i derived from
\f2\i0  MCF-7 WT, a B4-vs-WT paired call removes by construction the large pool of variants the two share \'97 which is most of them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Consequence for the thesis.
\f2\b0  The 6\'968\'d7 WT-vs-B4 burden gap reported in \'a75.3.1 is therefore driven substantially by this asymmetric calling design, not solely by the polyclonal-vs-monoclonal clonal architecture currently given as the explanation. The two explanations are entangled and the present data cannot fully separate them. This needs to be:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Documented in Methods (Chapter 3)
\f2\b0  \'97 state explicitly that WT was called tumour-only and B4 tumour\'96normal against matched WT, with the Sentieon command lines as evidence.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reframed in \'a75.3.1
\f2\b0  \'97 the absolute cross-genotype burden gap is partly a pipeline artefact; cross-genotype 
\f7\i absolute
\f2\i0  counts are not directly comparable. Within-genotype contrasts (WT-UN vs WT-APH; B4-UN vs B4-APH) and 
\f7\i proportional
\f2\i0  analyses remain valid.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Flagged in \'a75.3.2
\f2\b0  \'97 the coding-consequence 
\f7\i proportions
\f2\i0  are more robust to this than the absolute counts, but the populations compared are still different in kind (B4-private somatic vs WT-vs-reference).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
